Third-party attributions for the base PDF extractor (rust/src/extract/pdf/,
ADR-0017 step 2).

The PDF extractor contains NO code copied from the projects below. Each
technique was reimplemented from the description in
docs/research/2026-09-24-pdf-to-markdown.md (sections 3 and 8), which names
the upstream file. Where the research recorded a commit, it is pinned here.
Where it did not, the commit is marked "not pinned", meaning the upstream file
was not read at a fixed revision for this port. Before code (not just an idea)
is ported from any of these, pin the commit and add its licence text below.

Nothing AGPL, GPL or non-commercial is used anywhere in the stack.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
pdfium (BSD-3-Clause), loaded dynamically at runtime, not bundled
  https://pdfium.googlesource.com/pdfium
  Behaviour relied on: the U+0002 line-end hyphen marker
  (core/fpdftext/cpdf_textpage.cpp, ProcessGenerateCharacter), the
  FPDF_StructTree_* structure tree, and FPDFText_* character boxes.

pdfium-render (MIT OR Apache-2.0), a Cargo dependency
  https://github.com/ajrcarey/pdfium-render

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Ideas ported (reimplemented; no code copied)

Xberg (MIT) @ b4331e0
  https://github.com/xberg-io/xberg
  pdf/structure/pipeline.rs:5635-5891, collect_hyphen_witnesses /
  should_preserve_lexical_hyphen: document witnesses for line-end hyphens.
  -> src/extract/pdf/hyphen.rs

pdftext (Apache-2.0), commit not pinned
  https://github.com/datalab-to/pdftext
  postprocessing handle_hyphens: handling of pdfium's U+0002 marker.
  -> src/extract/pdf/hyphen.rs

LiteParse (Apache-2.0) @ b754dc3d
  https://github.com/run-llama/liteparse
  extract.rs "is-complex" routing reasons; markdown_layout/repetition.rs
  header/footer repetition; tables.rs ruled grid + inferred column tracks.
  -> src/extract/pdf/route.rs, src/extract/pdf/furniture.rs,
     src/extract/pdf/tables.rs

opendataloader-pdf (Apache-2.0) @ 323578b
  https://github.com/opendataloader-project/opendataloader-pdf
  TriageProcessor (conservative page triage), HeaderFooterProcessor.
  -> src/extract/pdf/route.rs, src/extract/pdf/furniture.rs

Docling (MIT), commit not pinned
  https://github.com/docling-project/docling
  reading_order_rb.py (rule-based reading order), rate_text_quality (text-
  layer soundness), heading levels ("a wrong level is worse than none").
  -> src/extract/pdf/order.rs, src/extract/pdf/route.rs,
     src/extract/pdf/headings.rs

Marker (Apache-2.0 since 2026-07-17), commit not pinned
  https://github.com/datalab-to/marker
  The >2% garbled-character threshold for an unsound text layer.
  -> src/extract/pdf/route.rs

Marker table_recon (Apache-2.0), commit not pinned
  https://github.com/datalab-to/marker
  Scored grid search over text-layer columns; the 0.75 acceptance threshold.
  -> src/extract/pdf/tables.rs

Xberg table_core.rs / table_reconstruct.rs (MIT) @ b4331e0
  Fake-table validators (one column, prose in columns, TOC).
  -> src/extract/pdf/tables.rs

pdfplumber lines strategy (MIT), commit not pinned
  https://github.com/jsvine/pdfplumber
  Ruling lines AND rectangle edges, snapped and intersected into cells.
  -> src/extract/pdf/tables.rs

GriTS (paper, arXiv 2203.12555; reference code microsoft/table-transformer
  src/grits.py, MIT, commit not pinned)
  GriTS-Con with the factored 2-D most-similar-substructure, reimplemented
  from the paper's algorithm. The reference file's AGPL `fitz` import is
  not used and was not read.
  -> src/checks.rs (grits_con), used by tables::choose and the contract

XY-Cut++ (paper, arXiv 2504.10258)
  Projection-profile XY-cut as the reading-order fallback. The paper's
  cross-layout pre-mask is NOT implemented.
  -> src/extract/pdf/order.rs
